# Client-side routing fallback.
#
# The app uses real paths (/revenue, /customers, /operations, /forecasting)
# rather than hash routes, so a static host has to serve index.html for any
# path it has no file for. Without this, a visitor who lands on or reloads
# anything but the root gets a 404 from the CDN before React ever runs.
#
# Existing files win: the host serves a real asset before consulting this rule,
# so /data/*.json and /assets/* are unaffected.
/*    /index.html   200
